# Terraform working files. None of these belong in the repository: the state is
# in S3 (backend.tf), the lock file for provider hashes is committed, and
# everything else is per-machine.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log

# tfvars can hold values, and a value in a file is a value one `git add -A` away
# from being public. Terraform holds no secret values by design (ADR-0010) — this
# is the belt to that braces. staging.tfvars and production.tfvars are the two
# exceptions: they are the whole story of what differs between the two
# environments (ADR-0158), and every value variables.tf lets them set is a
# non-secret configuration choice — never seek a "value" for one of the
# entries secrets.tf creates by adding one to either file.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!staging.tfvars
!production.tfvars

# Plan files. A plan contains the full resource graph, including any attribute a
# provider marked sensitive.
*.tfplan
